commit 58dbad667620e813fe283b3edce03b218c341516

C03: both memory figures are named with their labels for the system report, and forbidding a means is a prohibition (SYSTEM1547)

SYSTEM1545 measured that «Dime que version de Windows tengo y cuanta RAM tiene este PC. Usa Python.» reached a verified system.status but published no final: three drafts in a row called the usable total (16,54 GB) installed while the installed capacity read 17,18 GB, and the retries ran out. The memory instruction and the mislabelled_installed retry hint now carry both observed figures with their labels (installed_capacity is the RAM installed and the answer to how much RAM the PC has; total is what the system can use, never installed). «No uses Python.» got a greeting because «usar» heads no request: the prohibition projection admits usa/utiliza/emplea/use so forbidding a means is acknowledged as a prohibition. Registry-wide recogniser and prohibition diff: no literal changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


